# ~/.tmux-main.local: the windows bin/tmux-main builds when the "main" session does not exist.
# Bash, sourced by tmux-main. One line per window: window <name> <dir>...
# 1 dir: one pane. 2 dirs: left | right. 4 dirs: top left, top right, bottom left,
# bottom right. Splits are even. The first window is shown, with its first pane active.
# With no window lines, main is one window in $HOME. Write only window lines (and comments):
# other variables set here can clash with the ones tmux-main uses.
#
# window web  "$HOME/src/web" "$HOME/src/web"
# window api  "$HOME/src/api" "$HOME/src/worker" \
#             "$HOME/src/db"  "$HOME/src/infra"
